{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "האלך", :translit "ha'eilekh", :gloss "shall I go"} {:he "והכיתי בפלשתים", :translit "v'hikiti b'plishtim", :gloss "and I struck the Philistines"} {:he "האלך רמות גלעד", :translit "ha'eilekh ramot gil'ad", :gloss "shall I go to Ramoth Gilead"} {:he "דברי נביאים מתקיימים כדברי אורים ותומים", :translit "divrei n'vi'im mitkay'mim k'divrei urim v'tumim", :gloss "words of prophets are fulfilled like words of Urim and Thummim"} {:he "שמרים נתנבאה על משה קודם שנולד", :translit "sh'miryam nitn'be'ah al moshe kodem shenolad", :gloss "that Miriam prophesied about Moses before he was born"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["האלך" "והכיתי בפלשתים" "האלך רמות גלעד"]}], :frame {:text "Miriam is identified with Puah (Exodus 1:15) and is so named because she declared (הוֹדָה) that her mother would give birth to Moses (Sotah 12b). Amram divorced his wife after Pharaoh's decree, but Miriam prophesied that her mother would bear a son who would deliver Israel; when Moses was born, the house filled with light (Sotah 12b–13a). The Urim and Thummim are the priestly oracle through which God's word is consulted (Exodus 28:30).", :sources ["Sotah 12b" "Sotah 13a" "Exodus 28:30" "Exodus 1:15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "נצים", :translit "n'tzim", :gloss "sparrows / birds of prey"} {:he "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת", :translit "l'has'ot galim n'tzim adim b'tzurah", :gloss "to bear desolation, birds of prey, witnesses of drought"} {:he "כי מתו כל האנשים המבקשים את נפשך", :translit "ki metu kol ha'anashim ha'm'vaksheim et naf'shekhah", :gloss "for all the men who sought your life are dead"} {:he "דתן ואבירם", :translit "datan v'aviram", :gloss "Dathan and Abiram"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["נצים" "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת (Kings)" "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת (Isaiah)"]}], :frame {:text "Dathan and Abiram were Moses's adversaries who instigated rebellion and were swallowed by the earth with Korah's company (Numbers 16:27–32). Jethro's announcement to Moses that 'all the men who sought your life are dead' (Exodus 4:19) is understood to refer to Dathan and Abiram, who lost their wealth and status (Sanhedrin 110a, Nedarim 64b). The Sages state that the wealth of Korah's faction was so vast that the earth could not swallow it and it had to be hammered in (Sanhedrin 110a). Sennacherib's campaign against Jerusalem is recounted in 2 Kings 18–19 and Isaiah 36–37.", :sources ["Exodus 4:19" "Numbers 16:27" "Numbers 16:32" "Sanhedrin 110a" "Nedarim 64b" "2 Kings 18:13" "Isaiah 36:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["האלך" "והכיתי בפלשתים" "האלך רמות גלעד"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "האלך", :refs ["Exodus 2:7" "1 Samuel 23:2" "1 Kings 22:6"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והכיתי בפלשתים", :refs ["1 Samuel 23:2"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "האלך רמות גלעד", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["נצים" "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת (Kings)" "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת (Isaiah)"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "נצים", :refs ["Exodus 2:13" "2 Kings 19:25" "Isaiah 37:26"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת (Kings)", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "להשאות גלים נצים עדים בצורת (Isaiah)", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:05.083235248Z", :model "glm-5.2"}